From f94d0c2e02ef915417428cf53a8a0014a9dca0fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:50:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: adopt 2 audited levkropp fixes; fix 4 pre-existing
 backend bugs

Audited adoptions from levkropp/lccc (guilty-until-proven-innocent review):
- reuse_stack_loads_within_blocks (lev f958b6a fix e): only NOP a reload
  when the loaded register is proven dead afterwards (overwritten without
  intervening read, incl. MoveImm/MoveWide, or function end). Our pass
  order (propagate_register_copies BEFORE reuse_stack_loads) made the old
  unconditional NOP unsound: copy propagation could leave other readers
  of the reloaded register (strlen_bench-class segfault).
- propagate_address_aliases full-function rewrite (lev ed36c44): replace
  the same-block-window deletion with a whole-function scan that tracks
  source-register liveness and only deletes the defining mov when the
  source provably survives to every use.

Pre-existing bugs found & fixed during the audit (all reproduced on main):
1. ARM emit_reg_to_acc missing reg_cache.invalidate_acc(): the default
   emit_gep path (reg-homed base after LICM GlobalAddr hoisting) left a
   stale acc-cache entry, so emit_load_operand skipped loading the offset
   and computed base+base -> SIGSEGV (hash_table benchmark at -O2).
   x86-64/i686 already invalidate at the same point.
2. ARM ICE 'invalid ARM register index': integer BinOp dest with an FP
   register home reached callee_saved_name. Filter FP-homed dests in the
   register-direct ALU path; stage FP-homed sources through x0 in
   operand_to_callee_reg (fmov handled by operand_to_x0).
3. ARM emit_load_indexed_impl paired ldrsw with a W destination register
   for I32 GP-homed dests -- assembler error (ldrsw sign-extends into 64
   bits and only accepts X). Use the X name for ldrsw.
4. FP constant pool used '.align 16' which on AArch64/RISC-V gas means
   2^16 = 64KiB per constant: massive .rodata bloat that pushed the pool
   out of ldr-literal +/-1MB range (R_AARCH64_LD_PREL_LO19 truncation at
   static link). Emit '.p2align 4' (16 bytes on every gas target).

New regression tests: arm_gep_regbase_acc_cache.c (bug 1),
arm_fp_homed_int_binop.c (bugs 2/3/4 combined).

Validation: 1005/1005 unit, 50/50 correctness, 390/390 x86 regression,
ARM regression 239 pass (was 230 on main; 7 pre-existing failures fixed,
0 new), x86-64 fuzz 300/300, m32 fuzz 200/200, aarch64 fuzz O1 60/60
clean, O2 mismatches 24 -> 12 (rest pre-existing, under investigation).
